# Conditions

Conditions is a conceptual tool or principle that helps understand and navigate complex situations. It provides a mental shortcut or framework for making sense of patterns and relationships in the world.

The model is described as universally applicable and serves as a meta-level abstraction for recognizing how different factors, contexts, and states influence outcomes and decisions. It overlaps with related mental models such as [[settings]], [[environment]], and [[planning]], though its specific focus is on identifying and understanding the conditions under which judgments, predictions, or decisions improve.

The model draws on James Surowiecki's *The Wisdom of Crowds*, which explores how collective intelligence can outperform individual judgment under certain conditions—suggesting that "conditions" as a mental model may relate to understanding when and why groups or systems produce better results than individuals.

This entry is underdeveloped with moderate confidence (0.7). Further elaboration is needed to clarify how Conditions differs from existing mental models like [[settings]] or [[environment]].
